## Features

### 🚫 Blocklist

Add channels you don't want to see. Cards from those channels will be automatically hidden on the homepage, subscriptions feed, search results, and other listing pages.

**How to add:**
- **Manual input**: Fill in the channel name (required) and `@handle` (optional) in the panel form, then click Add
- **Quick button**: Hover over a video card — an action bar slides up from the bottom. Click 🚫 to block instantly
- **Three-dot menu**: If set to "Three-dot menu" mode, click the video's ⋮ menu and select "YtFC: Hide this channel"

**Tags**: Each channel can have tags for easier categorization (e.g., "Ad accounts", "Farm channels").

---

### ⭐ Whitelist

Add channels you trust or want to protect. Whitelisted channels are never affected by any filter rule — they won't be caught by the blocklist, keywords, or any other filter.

**Whitelist-only mode**: Enable "Show only whitelisted channels" in ⚙️ Settings. Once enabled, all channels except those in the whitelist will be hidden. Ideal for parental controls or a minimal viewing experience.

---

### 🎬 Video Blocklist

Block specific video IDs without needing to block the entire channel. Common use cases: hiding specific controversial videos or blocking episodes you're not interested in.

- Accepts a video ID (11 characters) or a full YouTube URL
- Once added, the block is **always enforced** and is not controlled by the Filter Scope matrix
- Accessing the video directly via URL will also show a block screen (requires "Force Block" to be enabled in Settings)

---

### 🔤 Keyword Filter

Filter videos based on keywords found in their title or description. Keywords are managed in **groups** — each group can be individually enabled or disabled.

**Creating a keyword group:**
1. Click "＋ Add Group" and enter a group name
2. Select the scope: title, description, or both
3. Add keywords within the group
4. Make sure the group toggle is set to "Enabled"

**Group priority**: Groups higher in the list take priority. Drag to reorder.

