## Advanced Features

### Filter Scope (Advanced)

Filter Scope lets you specify which YouTube page types each filter rule applies to. It's designed for users who need fine-grained control.

#### How to Enable

1. Go to ⚙️ **Settings**
2. Scroll to the bottom and check "**Enable Filter Scope (Advanced)**"
3. Click "💾 Save Settings"
4. A new "🎯 **Filter Scope**" tab will appear — click it to configure

#### Understanding the Matrix

The interface shows an **11 rules × 7 pages** matrix:

**Page types:**

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| 🏠 Home | YouTube homepage |
| 📨 Subscriptions | Subscriptions feed |
| 🔍 Search | Search results page |
| 🎬 Watch page | Recommendations sidebar while watching a video |
| 📺 Channel page | When visiting a specific channel |
| 🔥 Trending | Trending videos page |
| 📄 Other | Any other page |

**Rule types:**
Channel Blocklist, Video Blocklist, Keywords, Members-only, Live/Upcoming, Fundraiser, Upload Date, View Count, Language, Duration, Channel Posts.

#### How to Use

- **Click a cell**: Toggle the rule on/off for that page type (active = colored, inactive = gray)
- **"✓ All On" at row end**: Enable this rule for all page types
- **"✕ All Off" at row end**: Disable this rule for all page types
- **"Reset all to enabled" button**: Restore defaults (all rules apply to all pages)
- **Current page**: Highlighted with a special style so you can see where you are in the matrix

#### Example Use Cases

**Example 1 — Allow seeing blocked channels on their own channel page**
> Uncheck "Channel Blocklist" × "Channel page"
> → When visiting a blocked channel's page, their videos are still visible; but they remain hidden on the homepage and other listing pages

**Example 2 — Apply keyword filter only on the homepage**
> For the "Keywords" rule, keep only "Home" checked, uncheck all other pages
> → Keyword filters won't interfere when you're specifically searching for something

**Example 3 — Don't filter live streams on the subscriptions feed**
> Uncheck "Live / Upcoming" × "Subscriptions"
> → Live streams from subscribed channels will appear in your subscriptions feed, but not on the homepage

