### Regex Mode

Keyword groups support JavaScript Regular Expressions, giving you more flexible pattern matching for video titles and descriptions.

#### How to Enable

When adding a keyword inside a group, check the "**Regex**" checkbox to enable regex mode for that keyword.

#### Rules

- **No need** to wrap the pattern in `/` slashes or add flags like `/i`
- Matching is **case-insensitive** by default
- Backslashes (`\`) can be entered directly — no extra escaping needed

#### Common Examples

| Pattern | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `(ad\|sponsored\|paid)` | Title contains "ad", "sponsored", or "paid" |
| `(stock\|invest\|crypto)` | Title mentions any finance-related term |
| `EP\.?\d+` | Episode number formats: EP1, EP.1, EP 1, etc. |
| `^(?!.*official).*$` | Title does **not** contain "official" (negative lookahead) |
| `\d{4}` | Title contains a 4-digit number (e.g., a year) |
| `(LIVE\|STREAM\|streaming)` | Various live stream indicators |

#### Tips

- Regex applies only to the **individual keyword** where it's enabled; other keywords in the same group continue to use plain text matching
- If a pattern has invalid syntax (e.g., unmatched parentheses), the keyword automatically falls back to plain text matching
- For best performance, prefer `(a|b|c)` patterns over complex lookaheads

