### Kids Mode Setup

By combining multiple features, you can create a "whitelist-only + automatic dangerous content filtering" child-friendly browsing environment.

> ⚠️ **Important Disclaimer:** This script only filters video cards on listing pages (homepage, search, recommendations). It cannot block direct URL navigation to a video, and it cannot analyze the actual content of videos. **Strongly recommended to use alongside YouTube Kids, parental control software (e.g., Google Family Link), or router-level DNS filtering.**

#### Complete Setup Steps

**Step 1 — Build a whitelist**
Go to the ⭐ **Whitelist** tab and add every channel your child is allowed to watch.
For example: @PBSKids, @SesameStreet, @CocomelonOfficial

**Step 2 — Enable whitelist-only mode**
Go to ⚙️ **Settings** and turn on "⭐ Show only whitelisted channels".
After enabling, all channels except those in the whitelist will be hidden.

**Step 3 — Block live streams**
In Settings, under "📡 Live / Upcoming", enable both:
- Hide live streams
- Hide upcoming / scheduled premieres

Live chat in streams is a common risk vector — block them entirely.

**Step 4 — Create a dangerous content keyword group**
Go to 🔤 **Keywords**, create a group named "Dangerous Content", and set scope to "Title":

Add keywords such as:
```
violence, blood, horror, adult, gambling, weapons, drugs
```

For more efficiency, enable Regex mode and enter:
```
(violence|gore|horror|adult|gambling|18\+|explicit)
```

**Step 5 (Recommended) — Restrict video age**
In Settings, enable "📅 Upload Date" and set it to hide videos uploaded more than 30 days ago.
This helps prevent the algorithm from surfacing old controversial content.

**Step 6 (Recommended) — Language filter**
In Settings, enable "🌐 Language Filter", choose "Show only selected languages", and check only your child's native language.
This effectively filters out most foreign-language content.

**Step 7 (Recommended) — Set a PIN lock**
In Settings, set up a "PIN Lock" to prevent your child from changing the filter settings.

#### Advanced Setup with Filter Scope

After enabling Filter Scope (Advanced), you can fine-tune kids mode further:

- **Home, Subscriptions, Search**: Enable all rules
- **Watch page sidebar**: Enable all rules to prevent inappropriate recommendations while watching
- **Channel page**: You can relax the "Channel Blocklist" rule so parents can still browse a specific channel to review it

